  "limitations": [
    "F135 gas flow, constant effective specific heat, cooling, heat capacity and radiation inputs are declared estimates; no measured F135 thermal station, alloy, coating or spatial wall calibration.",
    "One uniform effective metal state cannot represent distinct liner, flameholder and petal temperatures. Dry operation may legitimately have little visible incandescence.",
    "Surface spectral integration produces physical luminance for an assumed grey emissivity, but scene exposure and display reference are not photometrically calibrated.",
    "Flame composition, soot contribution, spatial expansion and band weights remain assumed; temperature alone cannot determine a unique flame spectrum.",
    "Native legacy EGT and finite fuel-flow rundown are unchanged. The existing renderer fuel/spool gate can retain faint dry gas emission during rundown; hardware heat is independent.",
    "Full app CI and native/material tests pass; current GPU pixels, device performance and real-aircraft agreement have not been qualified."
  ]
